From fda8ca8522eb8a548b3fd253ec50d3778708dc58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:28:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui-sidebar): refresh the mirror on the heartbeat only
 while a TUI reads it

Every loaded folder rebuilt its TUI sidebar snapshot and rewrote the mirror file
every 2 s, even when no TUI was attached (an app-managed backend never has one).
With 22 idle folders that cost about 12 % of a core and up to 0.4 s event-loop
stalls. The TUI now touches a reader lease next to the mirror when it reads; the
heartbeat refreshes only while the lease is fresh. Event-driven flushes are
unchanged, and a TUI that attaches later sees a fresh mirror within one heartbeat.
